The sample herd is made up, by the author's own herd simulator; no real farm's records are in this repository.

Figures and their sources:
- Energy-corrected milk: 0.327 x milk + 12.95 x fat + 7.65 x protein, in lb (Tyrrell and Reid, 1965; Orth, 1992).
- Predicted dry matter intake: National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine (2021), Nutrient
  Requirements of Dairy Cattle, 8th revised edition, equation 2-1.
- 21-day pregnancy rate: counted the way DairyComp 305's BREDSUM report counts it.
- What a ration holds, where the farm has no analyses of its own: the NASEM (2021) feed library, from the nasem_dairy
  package (Fieguth, Innes and Cant). Those values are NASEM's and keep NASEM's terms (academic use with acknowledgment;
  commercial use needs NASEM's release), not this project's licence: see dairytools/data/NOTICE-nasem.md.

